# HALLYU — FRONTEND & BACKEND ENGINEERING RULES

VERSION 1.0
SYSTEM-WIDE IMPLEMENTATION CONSTITUTION

This document defines the non-negotiable engineering rules for building Hallyu across both frontend and backend.

Use this document together with:

1. Hallyu_Final_Integrated_Master_Build_Specification.md
2. HALLYU_BUILD_PROMPT.md
3. blueprints/
4. This document

==================================================
1. SOURCE-OF-TRUTH HIERARCHY
==================================================

When documents, images, or implementation assumptions disagree, follow this priority:

1. MASTER SPECIFICATION
   Defines product behavior, scope, rules, permissions, architecture, data model,
   security requirements, and MVP boundaries.

2. FRONTEND & BACKEND ENGINEERING RULES
   Defines how the frontend and backend must be implemented and connected.

3. BUILD PROMPT
   Defines the coding-agent execution process.

4. LINE-ART BLUEPRINTS
   Defines structural layout, component relationships, and interaction intent.

5. PREMIUM BLUEPRINT IMAGES
   Defines visual direction, hierarchy, composition, styling, and presentation.

A lower-priority source MUST NOT override a higher-priority requirement.

==================================================
2. BLUEPRINT RECONCILIATION PROTOCOL
==================================================

THIS IS A NON-NEGOTIABLE RULE.

The blueprint images are visual implementation references.

They are NOT the ultimate source of product truth.

IF A BLUEPRINT IMAGE CONFLICTS WITH THE WRITTEN PRODUCT SPECIFICATION:

DO NOT BLINDLY COPY THE IMAGE.

Instead:

1. Read the relevant section of the Master Specification.
2. Read the relevant section of HALLYU_BUILD_PROMPT.md.
3. Inspect the matching premium blueprint.
4. Inspect the matching line-art blueprint.
5. Identify the conflict.
6. Preserve the written product requirement.
7. Preserve the blueprint's visual language wherever compatible.
8. Adapt the visual implementation to satisfy the actual product requirement.
9. Never invent functionality simply because it appears in an image.
10. Never remove required functionality simply because it is absent from an image.
11. Never treat placeholder content in a blueprint as production data.
12. Never treat a screenshot as a complete functional specification.

The objective is NOT pixel-perfect reproduction of a static image.

The objective is:

PRODUCT CORRECTNESS
+
FUNCTIONAL CORRECTNESS
+
BACKEND CORRECTNESS
+
SECURITY
+
ACCESSIBILITY
+
VISUAL FIDELITY

If an image and the written specification disagree, the written specification wins.

If the visual design can be adapted without violating the specification, adapt it rather than ignoring the blueprint.

==================================================
3. WHAT BLUEPRINTS ARE ALLOWED TO DEFINE
==================================================

Blueprints primarily define:

- visual hierarchy
- layout
- spacing
- typography hierarchy
- component relationships
- navigation appearance
- card treatment
- visual density
- interaction intent
- brand language
- screen composition
- visual emphasis

Blueprints do NOT independently define:

- database architecture
- database permissions
- RLS
- authentication behavior
- authorization
- API contracts
- business logic
- spoiler authorization
- moderation policy
- production content
- analytics requirements
- security policy
- data retention
- backend architecture

A picture of a button does not automatically mean the product contains that feature.

A missing button in a picture does not mean a required feature should be removed.

==================================================
4. CORE ENGINEERING PRINCIPLE
==================================================

HALLYU IS ONE SYSTEM.

Frontend and backend must never be developed as unrelated layers.

Every meaningful feature must exist as a complete vertical slice:

UI
↓
State
↓
Service/Data Layer
↓
Backend
↓
Database
↓
Security/RLS
↓
Response
↓
UI State

A feature is NOT complete when only its UI exists.

A feature is NOT complete when only its database table exists.

A feature is NOT complete when only its API exists.

The complete user flow must work.

==================================================
5. FRONTEND ARCHITECTURE RULES
==================================================

Use React Native + Expo as defined by the Master Specification.

Maintain clear separation between:

- screens
- navigation
- reusable components
- feature modules
- hooks
- state
- services
- Supabase integration
- utilities
- types
- validation
- analytics

Do not put large amounts of business logic directly inside screen components.

Keep components focused and reusable.

Repeated UI patterns MUST become reusable components.

Examples:

- PostCard
- UserRow
- DramaCard
- ActorCard
- EpisodeRow
- CommunityRow
- ReactionBar
- SpoilerGate
- MediaViewer
- LoadingState
- EmptyState
- ErrorState
- Button
- Input
- Chip
- Tab
- BottomSheet

Do not duplicate nearly identical logic across multiple screens.

==================================================
6. DESIGN SYSTEM RULES
==================================================

All production UI must use centralized design tokens.

Do not scatter arbitrary values throughout the application.

Centralize:

- colors
- typography
- spacing
- radii
- shadows
- elevation
- animation timing
- icon sizing
- touch targets

Current Hallyu visual baseline:

Dark surface:
#0F0F0F

Brand gradient:
#4A1C6E → #2D6CDF

Accent:
#FF6B6B

Typography:
Inter or equivalent modern sans-serif.

Cards:
Approximately 12px radius.

Spacing:
Approximately 16px internal spacing baseline.

These values are visual baselines, not permission to hard-code every screen.

They must be centralized and adjustable.

==================================================
7. NAVIGATION RULES
==================================================

The five primary destinations remain:

1. Home
2. Explore
3. Create
4. Notifications
5. Profile

Do not add additional primary navigation destinations unless explicitly required by the Master Specification.

Secondary destinations may use:

- navigation stacks
- modal screens
- sheets
- contextual navigation
- deep links

Moderation/admin functionality must remain permission-gated.

==================================================
8. REAL DATA RULE
==================================================

Production UI MUST consume real backend data.

Forbidden:

- fake JSON pretending to be a finished feature
- hard-coded follower counts
- hard-coded likes
- fake comments
- fake notifications
- fake follows
- fake moderation results
- fake authenticated users
- fake successful mutations
- static production data presented as live data
- buttons that visually work but perform no real operation

Development seed data is allowed ONLY when clearly treated as seed/development data.

==================================================
9. BACKEND ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

Use Supabase/PostgreSQL as defined by the Master Specification.

The backend must support the product's required entities, including:

- users
- profiles
- preferences
- follows
- blocks
- mutes
- dramas
- episodes
- actors
- cast
- genres
- watch progress
- posts
- post media
- drama tags
- episode tags
- hashtags
- mentions
- comments
- reactions
- reposts
- bookmarks
- communities
- community members
- community roles
- episode discussions
- official accounts
- verification
- notifications
- notification preferences
- reports
- moderation actions
- moderation logs
- audit logs

Do not create unnecessary duplicate sources of truth.

==================================================
10. DATABASE RULES
==================================================

Critical application state must live in the database.

Examples:

- follows
- watched episodes
- watching status
- post ownership
- reactions
- bookmarks
- comments
- community membership
- moderation decisions
- permissions
- notification state

Schema changes MUST use versioned migrations.

Never rely on undocumented manual database changes.

Use appropriate:

- foreign keys
- unique constraints
- check constraints
- indexes
- timestamps
- deletion behavior
- referential integrity

Avoid:

- N+1 queries
- unbounded queries
- fetching entire tables
- unnecessary columns
- huge client-side datasets
- client-side filtering of massive datasets

Use:

- pagination
- indexed queries
- server-side filtering
- deterministic ordering
- selective data retrieval

==================================================
11. SECURITY AND RLS
==================================================

SECURITY MUST NEVER DEPEND ONLY ON THE FRONTEND.

Hiding a button is NOT authorization.

Every protected operation must be protected server-side.

Use Row Level Security where appropriate.

Users may only:

- read permitted data
- modify resources they own
- perform actions allowed by their role
- access communities they are permitted to access
- perform moderation actions when authorized

Spoiler restrictions must not be bypassable through direct database access.

Moderator/admin functionality must be server-authorized.

Private-account rules must be server-enforced.

Private-community rules must be server-enforced.

Never expose service-role credentials to the mobile application.

Never ship private API secrets inside the frontend bundle.

==================================================
12. AUTHENTICATION RULES
==================================================

Authentication must use the configured Supabase authentication system.

Handle:

- sign up
- sign in
- sign out
- session restoration
- expired sessions
- password recovery
- authentication errors
- account deletion
- account state changes

Never assume authentication simply because a screen is visible.

Every protected backend operation must validate the authenticated identity.

==================================================
13. SPOILER SYSTEM RULES
==================================================

Spoiler protection is a CORE HALLYU feature.

The frontend and backend must cooperate.

The system must understand:

- drama
- episode
- watched-through episode
- spoiler level
- episode discussion context

The frontend must provide appropriate spoiler gates.

The backend/data layer must prevent inappropriate disclosure where required.

A blurred UI element is NOT sufficient if protected information has already been exposed in the response.

Support appropriate controls for:

- reveal
- hide
- spoiler preferences
- muted dramas where supported

Spoiler behavior must remain consistent across:

- Home
- Explore
- Drama Hubs
- Episode Discussions
- Post Detail
- Search
- Notifications
- Profiles
- Communities
- Deep Links

==================================================
14. FEED RULES
==================================================

FOR YOU should initially use deterministic signals.

Relevant signals may include:

- followed users
- followed dramas
- followed actors
- followed communities
- interests
- watch history
- reactions
- comments
- bookmarks
- reposts
- freshness
- meaningful engagement

Do NOT build unnecessarily complex recommendation infrastructure before sufficient behavioral data exists.

FOLLOWING should prioritize the user's actual followed graph.

Every feed must respect:

- blocks
- mutes
- privacy
- moderation
- deletion
- spoiler rules

==================================================
15. POST CREATION
==================================================

Post creation must be a real transactional flow.

Expected flow:

Compose
↓
Validate
↓
Upload media if applicable
↓
Create post
↓
Attach drama/episode metadata
↓
Attach hashtags/mentions
↓
Publish
↓
Update feed

Handle partial failures.

Example:

If media upload succeeds but post creation fails, do not silently leave unmanaged files.

Mutations must provide meaningful success and failure states.

==================================================
16. COMMENTS AND REPLIES
==================================================

Comments must be real database records.

Enforce:

- ownership
- moderation
- deletion rules
- blocked-user behavior
- visibility
- spoiler behavior where applicable

Nested replies must follow the supported depth defined by the product specification.

Do not fake threaded discussions with local-only state.

==================================================
17. MEDIA RULES
==================================================

Follow the media requirements defined by the Master Specification.

Frontend responsibilities:

- validate basic file requirements
- show previews
- show upload progress
- handle cancellation
- handle failure
- avoid unnecessary uploads

Backend/storage responsibilities:

- validate ownership
- validate permissions
- enforce supported file constraints
- manage storage lifecycle
- support moderation
- remove orphaned media when appropriate

Do NOT implement:

- unauthorized streaming
- unauthorized downloading
- full-episode hosting
- piracy functionality

==================================================
18. REALTIME RULES
==================================================

Realtime should be used only where it materially improves the experience.

Appropriate examples:

- episode discussions
- new comments
- replies
- relevant notifications
- moderation queues where appropriate

Do not subscribe every screen to every realtime channel.

Realtime subscriptions must be:

- scoped
- cleaned up
- permission-aware
- reconnect-safe

==================================================
19. SEARCH RULES
==================================================

Search must be backend-driven.

Support relevant entities:

- dramas
- actors
- users
- communities
- posts
- hashtags

Use appropriate database search/indexing.

Do not download huge datasets and search them locally.

Search must respect:

- privacy
- blocks
- moderation
- visibility rules

==================================================
20. NOTIFICATION RULES
==================================================

Notifications must originate from real application events.

Examples:

- replies
- mentions
- follows
- episode releases
- community announcements
- relevant official updates

Notifications must support deep linking to the appropriate content.

Respect notification preferences.

Avoid accidental duplicate notifications.

==================================================
21. COMMUNITY RULES
==================================================

Community membership and permissions must be server-enforced.

Support appropriate roles such as:

- member
- moderator
- owner/admin where defined

Respect:

- private communities
- membership
- bans
- removals
- posting permissions
- moderation
- community rules

==================================================
22. OFFICIAL ACCOUNT RULES
==================================================

Official status must come from authoritative backend state.

Never create verification simply by rendering a checkmark.

Official accounts must use the permission model defined by the Master Specification.

==================================================
23. MODERATION RULES
==================================================

Moderation pipeline:

Report
↓
Classification
↓
Severity
↓
Automated action where appropriate
↓
Moderator queue
↓
Decision
↓
Audit log
↓
Appeal where supported

Moderation actions must be auditable.

Ordinary users must never gain access to moderator controls through frontend manipulation.

AI moderation must assist humans where required.

AI must not become an uncontrolled authority over high-impact enforcement.

==================================================
24. AI RULES
==================================================

AI is an assisting subsystem.

Possible services:

- spoiler classification
- toxicity classification
- spam detection
- duplicate detection
- post categorization
- hashtag suggestions
- translation
- recommendation assistance

Every AI subsystem must define:

- input
- output
- confidence
- fallback
- human-review behavior where applicable
- logging requirements
- privacy requirements

AI must NEVER:

- bypass RLS
- bypass authentication
- receive secrets from the frontend
- silently perform high-impact actions without defined safeguards

==================================================
25. LOADING / EMPTY / ERROR STATES
==================================================

Every asynchronous feature MUST support intentional:

- loading
- success
- empty
- partial failure
- complete failure
- retry
- intermittent connectivity

Do not use infinite spinners as error handling.

Do not show blank screens when data fails.

Optimistic updates must have rollback behavior.

==================================================
26. OFFLINE AND NETWORK RESILIENCE
==================================================

Design for real mobile networks.

The application must gracefully handle:

- slow connections
- temporary loss of connectivity
- failed uploads
- request timeouts
- realtime disconnects
- retry
- stale cached data

Do not assume permanent high-speed Wi-Fi.

==================================================
27. PERFORMANCE RULES
==================================================

Prioritize:

- fast initial render
- optimized images
- lazy loading
- pagination
- efficient lists
- caching
- minimal unnecessary requests
- efficient realtime subscriptions
- memory-conscious rendering

Do not hard-code the blueprint dimensions.

Real devices have different:

- screen sizes
- aspect ratios
- safe areas
- font scales
- keyboards
- accessibility settings

==================================================
28. ACCESSIBILITY RULES
==================================================

Accessibility is part of implementation, not a final polish step.

Support:

- screen readers
- semantic labels
- sufficient contrast
- dynamic text sizing
- usable touch targets
- reduced motion
- accessible forms
- meaningful errors

If a visual blueprint conflicts with accessibility, preserve the design intent while adapting the implementation for accessibility.

==================================================
29. DEEP LINK RULES
==================================================

Important Hallyu content must support deep links.

Examples:

- drama
- episode
- post
- profile
- community
- hashtag

Deep links must respect:

- authentication
- privacy
- permissions
- spoiler rules
- deleted content

==================================================
30. ANALYTICS RULES
==================================================

Measure meaningful product behavior.

Examples:

- onboarding completion
- drama follows
- episode discussion entry
- post creation
- comments
- reactions
- bookmarks
- reposts
- follows
- community joins
- notification engagement
- retention

Do not collect unnecessary personal information.

Analytics must never become a dependency that prevents core product functionality.

==================================================
31. FEATURE FLAGS
==================================================

Deferred functionality should be isolated behind feature flags where appropriate.

Examples:

- video
- polls
- DMs
- advanced AI
- future creator features

Disabled functionality must not leak unfinished production UI.

Do not silently activate deferred functionality.

==================================================
32. ENVIRONMENT AND SECRETS
==================================================

Maintain separate development, testing and production environments.

Never commit:

- private API keys
- service-role keys
- database passwords
- private credentials
- production secrets
- user secrets

Use secure environment configuration.

==================================================
33. DATA CONSISTENCY
==================================================

The backend is authoritative.

Frontend state must reconcile with backend state.

